The separately scoped coding benchmark adapter uses only the four pinned model
TOMLs for GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Luna, GLM-5.3 and GLM-5.3-Flash at models.dev
commit 3fb4bb98e633ff1af1b94f84ba07c8549e859aa8. The exact-revision MIT
LICENSE covers these model records, including their benchmark metadata. Only
DeepSWE and SWE-Marathon rows are normalized; each cited provider/model-card
reference and reported configuration is retained. No upstream source page or
full benchmark dataset is copied. SWE-Marathon's separately published
leaderboard dataset has no verified reuse grant and is excluded from this scope.
GLM configuration facts are attributed to the pinned Z.ai model-card revisions
listed in CODING_BENCHMARK_COMPARISON.md; only the cited facts are retained.

Official Z.ai documents contribute original factual annotations and public
references only. Their source pages, images, examples and tables are not copied
into distributed artifacts. Public facts do not establish private account state,
entitlement, actual execution, permitted data sharing or inference authority.

Installed acceptance test reuse (MI #19): the offline collector pairing and
explicit-input fixture technique in tests/installed_router_cases.py adapt the
Apache-2.0 Scarcity Router tests/test_mi_consumer.py and tests/observation.py at
4162f6fa9f774beaf6e92d86b7ebc92f306da4bd:
https://forgejo.creatidy.com/BioMedical-IT/scarcity-router
These test adaptations are changed from the original fixture. The runner also
executes unchanged copies of those two tests from that exact source archive in
temporary staging, retaining the original repository LICENSE with the archive.
No foreign selector, validator, production implementation or public dataset is
vendored. The Apache-2.0 license is provided in this repository's LICENSE.

Terminal-Bench 4.0 selected result evidence originates from the four
`leaderboard/submissions/*.json` files at
`harbor-framework/terminal-bench` commit
`6964e9252c90227fc1cfa26cbc59aee4134792e4`. These are repository submission
contributions under its root Apache-2.0 License (Sections 2 and 5); the
maintainer submission workflow and per-file provenance are recorded in
`CODING_BENCHMARK_COMPARISON.md`. This is the rights basis for these selected
summary observations, not an assumption that a code license covers unrelated
leaderboard data. Terminal-Bench 4.0 task content and raw Harbor Hub trial
payloads/trajectories are not copied. Source-job identifiers are retained only
as citations from the licensed submission records. The benchmark result rows,
metrics, source filters and candidate configurations are attributed to the
official Terminal-Bench submission repository at the pinned revision.
